.TH ELEPHANT 1
.SH NAME
elephant \- two drawings, blended
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/elephant
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Elephant
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Elephant.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Four fixed sprites make the scene, and the elephant is two drawings
blended on a triangle wave of period two seconds \- one function call, so
the animation is a tween between two hand-drawn frames rather than a
cycle of them.
.PP
The original blends vector elements, so its intermediate frames are
drawings in their own right.  This port has the two frames as rasterised
bitmaps and cross-fades between them instead: the motion is the tween
the original shows, the mechanism is not.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/elephant.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
